# End-of-turn worker brief (Cursor main agent)

When this Cursor chat is the **Sume main agent**, **every turn ends**
with a markdown **표** of current worker status. Do not skip it because
the turn was “just a rule edit”, a short answer, or a canvas refresh.

Chat copy matches Chase’s language (Korean in this desk). Identifiers
stay English (`#4790`, `session_id`, `bcId`).

This is **not** a poll loop. One-shot reconcile, then the table, then
stop. No `AwaitShell` / `sleep` watchers.

## Two tables (always)

### 1. Desk — `지금`

Live count = intersection of:

- Cursor terminals with **alive PID** + still-running worker command
- Live `claude-human-stream` / `agent-human-stream` / `grok -p`

Job = Shell `description` / terminal title
(`Opus : <slug> (#N)` / `Grok : <slug> (#N)`).

| Job | Issue | 모델 | session_id | 시그널 |
|-----|-------|------|------------|--------|

Empty live set → one row: `—` / `데스크 라이브 없음`.

Finished this turn → do **not** keep them in `지금`. Mention in a
one-line 스테이징 note under the tables if useful.

### 2. Cursor Cloud — **무조건**

If `cursor-cloud` MCP is available this turn, call
`list-cloud-agents` (this env / same repo). **Every agent that is
still operating must appear as its own row.** Never omit a Cloud
worker because the desk table already has Opus/Grok.

Must-list statuses (each row, no collapsing):

- `RUNNING`
- `WAITING_FOR_BACKGROUND_WORK`
- `NOT_YET_STARTED`
- this run (`run-info` `bcId`) even if the filter would hide it

Also list non-`internal` **IDLE** boxes that are still alive
(`desktop` / `web` / `setup` / named product runs). `source: internal`
computerUse leftovers that are **IDLE** may be **one count row**
(`internal IDLE N`) — not if any of those is `RUNNING`.

| Name | status | source | model | bcId / URL | 시그널 |
|------|--------|--------|-------|------------|--------|

Link `https://cursor.com/agents/<bcId>` (or the tool’s `url` field).

If MCP is missing / auth-failed: say so in the Cloud table, still
list **this** run when `run-info` works.

## When

Last user-visible block of the turn — after the answer, after canvas
refresh. Same turn as any launch / completion / steer.

Canvas (`active-workers-canvas.mdc`) is the board; **this table is
mandatory in chat** even when the canvas is current.

## Non-goals

- Not a substitute for completion-notification monitoring
- Do not dump full `list-cloud-agents` JSON into chat
- Codex / Claude Code as main agent: ignore this rule (Cursor-only)
